-- A pushed particle whose class the program defines no handler for is
-- dropped, and the program carries on. Decided 2026-08-28, replacing the
-- opposite rule this file used to pin (`fail_inbound_unhandled.code`).
--
-- The reason is `Log`/`Exception`: a module speaks first on its own
-- initiative, so a diagnostic nobody asked to hear is not a mistake by the
-- program. Making it fatal would mean every program linking a module that
-- *might* report something has to handle it, whether it cares or not.
--
-- The cost, accepted knowingly: a module pushing a mistyped class is now
-- invisible rather than loud.
link "native_modules/test_events.so" as ev

emit Start { "value": 3 } to ev get started
assert started.value = 3

-- Three Ticks were queued and all three went nowhere. Reaching here at all
-- is the assertion; `emit ... to this` is unchanged and still errors on a
-- class nothing handles (fail_handler_unknown.code).
assert 1 + 1 = 2
